Cross-JWT and token type confusion

Cross-JWT (or token type) confusion occurs when validation rules fail to distinguish token kinds, allowing a token issued for one purpose (such as an ID or password-reset token) to be accepted as another (such as an access token). Overlapping claims or shared signing keys are common enabling conditions (see RFC 8725 §2.8).

